,"gamedev","html5","ios","java","libgdx","linux","macosx","windows"],"visibility":"public","forks":6523,"open_issues":320,"watchers":24609,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Versions affected: master:1.6.6-SNAPSHOT and goes back to 1.5.0 (haven't tested 1.4.x)\nI'm using color tags to emphasize keywords and f.draw handles spaces before tags poorly even in a single line string. I don't know if spaces are skipped or if it's a glyphrun bug.\n\nI haven't tried it with fixed width fonts.\n\n``` Java\n        f.draw(batch, \"...blah blah[RED] BINGO[] blah blah... \",300,300);\n        f.draw(batch, \"...blah blah [RED]BINGO []blah blah... \",300,270);\n```\n\n![bug](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/8305672/10016787/1aa8d3d0-6132-11e5-99c3-3dece750a2d6.png)\n\nAdding 1 extra space seems to work but it's not elegant.\n\n``` Java\n        f.draw(batch, \"...blah blah  [RED]BINGO  []blah blah... \",300,240);\n```\n\nEdit: Provided test code & assets in my last comment. Please review.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgdx/libgdx/issues/3432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgdx/libgdx/issues/3432/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]